  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher chokepoint transit volumes raise immediate FX receipts for oil-exporting economies (and reduce payment-side volatility for importers), supporting those exporters' currencies and putting upward pressure on their exchange-rate levels versus major currencies.</data>
