<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="taiwan_cross_strait::trade_restriction_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising operational/political pressure to prevent rapid military technology transfer observed in the Russia–Ukraine war prompts governments to expand export controls and licensing on dual‑use and advanced technologies that affect cross‑strait trade policy.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising political and operational pressure increases policymakers' appetite to impose broader and stricter export controls and licensing on dual‑use and strategic technologies between the US and China.</data>
