<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" target="global_currency_friction::policy_rate_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained net inflows into a jurisdiction's tech/industrial sectors relax external financing constraints and currency pressure, reducing the need for monetary authorities to hike policy rates (or allowing them to cut) to stabilize markets and fund the economy.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_currency_friction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased cross‑border capital into relevant manufacturers or trading intermediaries enables ramped production or bulk purchases of complete UAVs and rapid export to combat actors, raising the frequency of drone strikes as inventories and production are expanded.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" target="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A fall in cross-border capital (driven by sanctions, tighter screening, or risk aversion tied to the rivalry) immediately reduces net inbound equity and direct investment from Chinese and third‑party investors into Taiwanese industrial and tech firms.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
</edge>
