<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_resilience" target="russia_ukraine_war::component_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved supply‑chain resilience (alternative qualified suppliers, validated second‑source production and logistics redundancies) directly sustains flows of drone parts and spares into combat zones despite sanctions or interdictions, increasing component availability quickly.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_resilience" target="taiwan_cross_strait::advanced_tech_capability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved resilience (diversified suppliers, redundant logistics, stockpiles) reduces production interruptions and loss of engineering staff, thereby preserving and modestly enhancing Taiwan's cumulative high‑end technical know‑how and production capability.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
</edge>
