<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::advanced_tech_capability" target="russia_ukraine_war::component_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Increases in Taiwan's high-end semiconductor and sensor production capacity directly raise the global supply of chips and guidance components that are re‑exported or incorporated into drones used by actors in the Russia–Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::advanced_tech_capability" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::adv_manuf_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">When Taiwanese firms (e.g., leading foundries) increase process-node know‑how and deploy it in existing fabs, they directly raise operable advanced-manufacturing throughput (semiconductor wafer starts and advanced module output) available to global markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="taiwan_cross_strait::technology_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="taiwan_cross_strait::logistics_route_diversit" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="taiwan_cross_strait::trade_restriction_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="global_currency_friction::exchange_rate_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in Taiwan's manufacturing export shipments increases foreign‑currency (USD) inflows into the region, easing demand for safe‑haven currencies and putting downward pressure on major USD bilateral exchange rates (i.e., USD weakens vs affected Asian currencies).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">global_currency_friction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="hormuz_standoff::choke_point_transit_volu" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden fall in Taiwan-origin manufactured exports signals weaker global industrial activity and reduces near-term refinery feedstock and refined-product demand, producing fewer tanker loadings and a measurable drop in transit volume through key chokepoints such as the Strait of Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::manufacturing_export_flo" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained high-volume outbound shipments of critical components (chips, modules) from Taiwanese manufacturers directly reduce upstream shortages and bottlenecks, thereby improving the ability of US/China technology value chains to maintain production and recover from disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
