<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" target="global_currency_friction::fx_intervention_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger net inbound investment capital into Taiwan reduces bilateral capital‑flight and depreciation pressure on regional currencies, lowering the frequency and scale of official FX intervention by regional central banks seeking to defend exchange rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">global_currency_friction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::component_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased cross‑border investment into Taiwanese and regional subcontractors expands manufacturing capacity and inventories for drone subsystems, which after lead times become available to global markets that can supply the Russia–Ukraine conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increases in cross‑border investment originating in or routed through Taiwanese firms (e.g., project finance, JV capital for fabs abroad) directly raise measurable cross‑border capital flows into PRC or regional technology sectors involved in the US–China rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
