  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in major policy rates raise global borrowing costs and compress venture and project returns, prompting investors and banks to scale back cross‑border financing for capital‑intensive advanced‑manufacturing and semiconductor investments linked to US–China competition.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_currency_friction</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
