<edge source="global_currency_friction::fx_funding_stress" target="hormuz_standoff::choke_point_transit_volu" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute cross‑currency funding stress raises dollar/working‑capital costs for shipowners, charterers and insurers, causing cancellations, delays or rerouting of tanker voyages and thereby reducing tanker transit volumes through Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_currency_friction</data>
  <data key="d40">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_currency_friction::fx_funding_stress" target="russia_ukraine_war::component_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising cross‑currency funding stress increases the cost and reduces the availability of foreign‑currency payments for Russian importers and third‑party intermediaries, choking off purchases of foreign drone components and subsystems.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_currency_friction</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_currency_friction::fx_funding_stress" target="taiwan_cross_strait::investment_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated cross‑currency funding stress raises the cost and availability constraints of dollar and other foreign funding for Taiwanese firms and foreign investors, causing immediate reductions or delays in cross‑border equity, debt and project finance into Taiwan.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_currency_friction</data>
  <data key="d40">taiwan_cross_strait</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_currency_friction::fx_funding_stress" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in cross‑currency funding stress raise hedging costs and cut dollar liquidity for overseas borrowers and investors, forcing suspension or cancellation of FDI, portfolio flows and project financing into tech and industrial projects tied to the US–China rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_currency_friction</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
